    "https://www.aalto.fi/en/open-positions/university-lecturer-or-senior-university-lecturer-wood-science": {
      "title": "University Lecturer or Senior University Lecturer, Wood Science",
      "description": "University Lecturer or Senior University Lecturer, Wood Science | Aalto University Skip to main content Sign of Change Sign of Change Donate Apply to Aalto Valitse sivuston kieli / Välj webbplatsens språk / Select site language EN FI Suomeksi SV Svenska EN English Search Log in Menu Close menu Student Guide For personnel Aalto community members please log in to see internal content Admissions and studies Apply to Aalto Find a study programme How to apply Scholarships and tuition fees Bachelor's admissions (programmes in Finnish and Swedish) Bachelor’s admissions (programmes in English) Master's admissions Doctoral admissions Campus life Events for applicants Chat with students Subscribe to newsletter Contact admission services Founder School: from students to founders Lifewide Learning Exchange students Research and art About our research and art Tenure track career system Doctoral education Research and learning infrastructures Research portal research.aalto.fi Rankings Schools and departments Schools School of Arts, Design and Architecture School of Business School of Chemical Engineering School of Electrical Engineering School of Engineering School of Science Departments Accounting & Business Law Applied Physics Architecture Art and Media Bioproducts and Biosystems Built Environment Chemical and Metallurgical Engineering Chemistry and Materials Science Civil Engineering Computer Science Design Economics Electrical Engineering and Automation Electronics and Nanoengineering Film, Television and Scenography Finance Industrial Engineering and Management Information and Communications Engineering Information and Service Management Management Studies Marketing Mathematics and Systems Analysis Energy and Mechanical Engineering Neuroscience and Biomedical Engineering Other units Language Centre Library - Learning Centre Collaboration Collaborate with us For alumni Corporate collaboration Aalto networking platform Entrepreneurship and innovations Cooperation with HEI and research institutes Collaboration with cities and regions Support us News and events Highlights News Events Aalto University Magazine OurBlogs Podcasts About us About Aalto University Our strategy Sustainability Code of Conduct Aalto Handbook Campus People and contact information For the media Careers Tools and services All tools (requires login) All services Most used tools Aalto AI Assistant Abacus-accounting Abacus-planning Asio (booking.aalto.fi) Halli Marketing Cloud MOT Kielipalvelu (language service) Neo People hub Phone book PowerBI report finder Salesforce (Service platform) Tiima Webmail Webropol Workday Most used services AI in Aalto Communications services HR services IT Services Learning services Occupational health Research and innovation services Teacher's Handbook Travel services For students Sisu MyCourses MyStudies Browse all courses Safety and emergencies Emergencies Safety and security observations Cyber Security Cyber Security incident report Other Aalto Space Aalto University Shop Brand library and design system Lunch menus EN FI SV Apply to Aalto Donate Student Guide For personnel Aalto community members please log in to see internal content Log in Search Open positions University Lecturer or Senior University Lecturer, Wood Science 16.10.2026 Application closes on 30.11.2026 Unit School of Chemical Engineering Job category Other teaching and research personnel Aalto University is where science and art meet technology and business. We shape a sustainable future by making research breakthroughs in and across our disciplines, sparking the game changers of tomorrow and creating novel solutions to major global challenges. Our community is made up of 16 000 students and 5 200 employees, including more than 440 professors. Our campus is in Espoo, Greater Helsinki, Finland.  Diversity is part of who we are, and we actively work to ensure our community’s diversity and inclusiveness. This is why we warmly encourage qualified candidates from all backgrounds to join our community. The School of Chemical Engineering is one of the six schools of Aalto University. The Department of Bioproducts and Biosystems (Bio2) focuses on innovations and cutting-edge research to support the emerging bioeconomy. We are now looking for a University Lecturer or Senior University Lecturer in Wood Science Background The importance of wood and wood products as our main renewable materials for construction, furniture, and many other applications is growing rapidly in our transition to a more sustainable society. The forest-based industry is vital to the economy of Finland. To meet the expected future demand for professionals with expertise in wood, we are strategically expanding our wood teaching and research activities. Aalto University is unique, as it is the only place in Finland where it is possible to study wood science alongside architecture, design, and construction. Teaching at master’s level at Aalto University is mostly in English, and teaching at bachelor’s level is primarily in Finnish. Your role and goals We are looking for a highly motivated University Lecturer or Senior University Lecturer in Wood Science. The candidate’s role is mainly to teach wood science, both independently and in collaboration with Aalto professors and researchers in the field. With their expertise in wood science, the candidate will be actively involved in developing and improving the teaching curriculum at the School of Chemical Engineering. The ideal candidate must hold a doctoral degree in a relevant discipline and have a strong research background in the biology, chemistry, physics, and/or materials science of wood or a closely related subject with emphasis on future skills needed in industry. Furthermore, the candidate should have a track record in teaching and teaching development, alongside a commitment to teaching. Working with the senior academic staff responsible for wood science activities at the department, the candidate will contribute to the development of the wood science curriculum, in addition to developing teaching. In addition, the candidate is expected to conduct their own independent research, contributing to the strategic aims of the department. The candidate will also be expected to apply for funding to support future teaching developments and/or research. While it is expected that most of their responsibilities will be directly related to teaching, the candidate will also be active in research and supervising students at all levels (BSc, MSc, DSc). Expected qualifications and experience The candidate must have the following: Doctoral degree in a suitable field in relation to wood science (civil, mechanical, chemical engineering, forest engineering, chemistry, physics) Demonstrable teaching experience and commitment (e.g., lectures and laboratory work) Track record of research in wood science or a highly related field Excellent written and oral communication skills in English Minimum 5 ECTS (or equivalent) pedagogical studies for a university lecturer position and 25 ECTS for a senior university lecturer Specific future-oriented skills. For example: AI, Entrepreneurial, Business, Data-analysis, Circularity of wood products, etc. The following will be regarded as merits: Written and oral communication skills in Finnish and/or Swedish Knowledge of the Finnish university education system Knowledge of the Finnish woodworking industry Experience in teaching multidisciplinary student groups Experience in developing educational material Experience in raising funding for research and/or teaching Good publication track record and activity What we offer The selected candidate will be offered a permanent position in the lecturer career system. Their qualifications and experience will determine the candidate’s positioning in the lecturer career system. More information about the lecturer career system at Aalto University can be found here: https://www.aalto.fi/en/teaching-and-learning/lecturer-career-system Salary is determined according to the salary system of Aalto University, and it is based on the applicant's experience and qualifications. Our facilities are located at Aalto University Otaniemi campus in Espoo, Finland. The employment contract includes occupational health care, and Finland has a comprehensive social security system. Aalto University provides excellent learning and development opportunities and a commuter ticket benefit. Unisport offers versatile sports facilities and exercise services with a staff discount. Ready to apply? If you want to join our community, please submit your application through our online recruitment system no later than 30.11.2026 by using the link on Aalto University’s webpage (“Apply now”). If you are an Aalto employee, you should apply for the position via our internal HR system Workday (Internal Jobs) by using your existing Workday user account (not via the external webpage for open positions). To apply, please include the following documents in English and as a single pdf document: Motivation letter (1-page description of your motivation for applying for this position and why you would be a suitable candidate) CV, including a list of publications Teaching portfolio according to Aalto University’s guidelines - see Teaching portfolio guidelines for candidates Please see further instructions for preparing the application documents here: https://www.aalto.fi/en/teaching-and-learning/lecturer-career-system For further information about the position, please contact Professor Lauri Rautkari. In recruitment-related questions, please contact HR Partner Noora Katisko (firstname.lastname@aalto.fi). Want to know more about us and your future colleagues ? You can watch these videos: This is Aalto University! Aalto University – Towards a better world and Shaping a Sustainable Future Read more about working at Aalto: https://www.aalto.fi/en/careers-at-aalto andcheck out our new virtual campus experience: https://virtualtour.aalto.fi More about Aalto University: Aalto.fi youtube.com/user/aaltouniversity linkedin.com/school/aalto-university/ www.facebook.com/aaltouniversity instagram.com/aaltouniversity To view information about Workday Accessibility, please click here . Please see more of our Open Positions here. Interested? Apply now! Updated: 16.10.2026 Published: 16.10.2026 Share URL copied! Home Open positions University Lecturer or Senior University Lecturer, Wood Science Sign of Change Aalto University P.O. Box 11000 (Otakaari 1B) FI-00076 AALTO Switchboard: +358 9 47001 Follow us: Facebook LinkedIn Bluesky Instagram Youtube Snapchat Blogs Quicklinks Research and artistic outputs Library – Learning Centre Admissions Alumni Media IT services Open University Aalto University Shop Site index Latest News Events Careers Contact Campus maps Contact information Ethical channel – Whistleblowing For students Student Guide Webmail MyCourses MyStudies Sisu Together towards a better world. Support new ideas, research, work and leadership development towards a stronger Finland. Donate to Aalto University Privacy notice Cookie policy Feedback Accessibility statement Cookie settings Suomeksi Svenska English"
    },
    "https://www.aalto.fi/en/open-positions/doctoral-researcher-chemical-upgrading-of-polyphenols-for-advanced-functional-materials": {
      "title": "Doctoral researcher, chemical upgrading of polyphenols for advanced functional materials",
      "description": "Doctoral researcher, chemical upgrading of polyphenols for advanced functional materials | Aalto University Skip to main content Sign of Change Sign of Change Donate Apply to Aalto Valitse sivuston kieli / Välj webbplatsens språk / Select site language EN FI Suomeksi SV Svenska EN English Search Log in Menu Close menu Student Guide For personnel Aalto community members please log in to see internal content Admissions and studies Apply to Aalto Find a study programme How to apply Scholarships and tuition fees Bachelor's admissions (programmes in Finnish and Swedish) Bachelor’s admissions (programmes in English) Master's admissions Doctoral admissions Campus life Events for applicants Chat with students Subscribe to newsletter Contact admission services Founder School: from students to founders Lifewide Learning Exchange students Research and art About our research and art Tenure track career system Doctoral education Research and learning infrastructures Research portal research.aalto.fi Rankings Schools and departments Schools School of Arts, Design and Architecture School of Business School of Chemical Engineering School of Electrical Engineering School of Engineering School of Science Departments Accounting & Business Law Applied Physics Architecture Art and Media Bioproducts and Biosystems Built Environment Chemical and Metallurgical Engineering Chemistry and Materials Science Civil Engineering Computer Science Design Economics Electrical Engineering and Automation Electronics and Nanoengineering Film, Television and Scenography Finance Industrial Engineering and Management Information and Communications Engineering Information and Service Management Management Studies Marketing Mathematics and Systems Analysis Energy and Mechanical Engineering Neuroscience and Biomedical Engineering Other units Language Centre Library - Learning Centre Collaboration Collaborate with us For alumni Corporate collaboration Aalto networking platform Entrepreneurship and innovations Cooperation with HEI and research institutes Collaboration with cities and regions Support us News and events Highlights News Events Aalto University Magazine OurBlogs Podcasts About us About Aalto University Our strategy Sustainability Code of Conduct Aalto Handbook Campus People and contact information For the media Careers Tools and services All tools (requires login) All services Most used tools Aalto AI Assistant Abacus-accounting Abacus-planning Asio (booking.aalto.fi) Halli Marketing Cloud MOT Kielipalvelu (language service) Neo People hub Phone book PowerBI report finder Salesforce (Service platform) Tiima Webmail Webropol Workday Most used services AI in Aalto Communications services HR services IT Services Learning services Occupational health Research and innovation services Teacher's Handbook Travel services For students Sisu MyCourses MyStudies Browse all courses Safety and emergencies Emergencies Safety and security observations Cyber Security Cyber Security incident report Other Aalto Space Aalto University Shop Brand library and design system Lunch menus EN FI SV Apply to Aalto Donate Student Guide For personnel Aalto community members please log in to see internal content Log in Search Open positions Doctoral researcher, chemical upgrading of polyphenols for advanced functional materials 16.10.2026 Application closes on 5.11.2026 Unit School of Chemical Engineering Job category Doctoral Researchers Aalto University is where science and art meet technology and business. We shape a sustainable future by making research breakthroughs in and across our disciplines, sparking the game changers of tomorrow and creating novel solutions to major global challenges. Our community is made up of 16 000 students and 5 200 employees, including more than 440 professors. Our campus is in Espoo, Greater Helsinki, Finland.  Diversity is part of who we are, and we actively work to ensure our community’s diversity and inclusiveness. This is why we warmly encourage qualified candidates from all backgrounds to join our community. The School of Chemical Engineering is one of the six schools of Aalto University. The Department of Bioproducts and Biosystems (Bio2) focuses on innovations and cutting-edge research to support the emerging bioeconomy. The Bioproduct Chemistry group is now looking for a Doctoral researcher in chemical upgrading of polyphenols for advanced functional materials About the Bioproduct Chemistry group The Bioproduct Chemistry group, lead by Professor Monika Österberg, aims to replace fossil‑based materials with renewable biomaterials from natural resources, especially forest biomass. We specialize in bio‑based materials science and the surface chemistry of lignocellulosic materials, with emphasis on fundamental insights and interaction forces. Our research themes include: Renewable and recyclable materials from cellulose, lignin, and hemicelluloses Valorization of polyphenolic side streams and greener processes (e.g., mechanochemistry, surface modification) Interfacial phenomena and development of biobased barriers, foams, and emulsions Advanced textile recycling, including flotation‑based methods Learn more: https://www.aalto.fi/en/department-of-bioproducts-and-biosystems/bioproduct-chemistry Position description Are you excited about sustainability and renewable materials? Bark and lignin are abundant, underutilized feedstocks rich in polyphenols. When engineered to self‑assemble into spherical colloidal particles, these compounds can replace fossil‑based or harmful chemicals across coatings, packaging, emulsifiers, and other applications. In this PhD project, you will work at crossroads of natural products chemistry, material science, and industry, specifically: Develop efficient fractionation and modification routes for polyphenols, including solvent‑free reactive extrusion Establish structure–property–performance relationships linking chemical composition and particle size to application performance Combine wet‑chemistry characterization (e.g., 1H/13C/ 2D NMR, AFM, DLS, GPC, FTIR, zeta potential) with molecular modeling and machine learning Collaborate with international academic and industrial partners Who we’re looking for A curious, ambitious researcher with strong interest in organic andsurface chemistry, specifically lignin/polyphenol chemistry Problem‑solver with good time‑management and communication skills Advantageous (but not required): experience with surface‑sensitive techniques, synthetic and preparative organic chemistry,lignin analytics, colloids, polymer processing, programming (e.g., Python/R/Matlab), molecular simulation or machine learning Required qualifications Master’s degree in chemistry or chemical engineering Good written and spoken English, and ability to work in a multidisciplinary international team Hands‑on laboratory experience in relevant areas What we offer We offer a fixed-term contract initially for two years. During the first 6 months, you must apply for and receive the right to study in the doctoral programme in Chemical Engineering. After a successful evaluation by the end of the first 2-year contract, the contract can be extended. Extension of the contract is typically based on the progress evaluation, revised project plan and available funding. The starting salary for a Doctoral Researcher is about 3140 €/month (gross) Access to Aalto’s state‑of‑the‑art facilities in an international research group How to apply Please submit your application as a single PDF file through our online recruitment system by using the link on Aalto University’s webpage (“Apply now”): Cover letter (1–2 pages) describing your motivation, relevant experience, and fit for the position CV (including possible publications, presentations, and contact details of 1–3 referees) Transcript of records with grades, and diploma if available All materials must be in English and submitted via the online system. Email applications cannot be considered. If you are an Aalto employee, you should apply for the position via our internal HR system Workday (Internal Jobs) by using your existing Workday user account (not via the external webpage for open positions). Timeline and process Application deadline: November 5. 2026, but the position may be filled before the deadline. Preferred start date: As soon possible, or as agreed. Aalto University reserves the right, for justified reasons, to leave the position open, extend the application period, or consider candidates who have not applied within the application period. Contacts For further information about the research project and research environment/group, please contact Dr. Nicolò Pajer ( nicolo.pajer@aalto.fi ) or Prof. Monika Österberg ( monika.osterberg@aalto.fi ) Want to know more about us and your future colleagues ? You can watch these videos: This is Aalto University! Aalto University – Towards a better world and Shaping a Sustainable Future Read more about working at Aalto: https://www.aalto.fi/en/careers-at-aalto andcheck out our new virtual campus experience: https://virtualtour.aalto.fi About Finland Finland is a great place for living with or without family – it is a safe, politically stable and well-organized Nordic society. Finland is consistently ranked high in quality of life and was listed again as the happiest country in the world: World Happiness Report For more information about living in Finland: Aalto Careers for International Staff . More about Aalto University: Aalto.fi youtube.com/user/aaltouniversity linkedin.com/school/aalto-university/ www.facebook.com/aaltouniversity instagram.com/aaltouniversity To view information about Workday Accessibility, please click here . Please see more of our Open Positions here. Interested? Apply now! Updated: 16.10.2026 Published: 16.10.2026 Share URL copied! Home Open positions Doctoral researcher, chemical upgrading of polyphenols for advanced functional materials Sign of Change Aalto University P.O. Box 11000 (Otakaari 1B) FI-00076 AALTO Switchboard: +358 9 47001 Follow us: Facebook LinkedIn Bluesky Instagram Youtube Snapchat Blogs Quicklinks Research and artistic outputs Library – Learning Centre Admissions Alumni Media IT services Open University Aalto University Shop Site index Latest News Events Careers Contact Campus maps Contact information Ethical channel – Whistleblowing For students Student Guide Webmail MyCourses MyStudies Sisu Together towards a better world. Support new ideas, research, work and leadership development towards a stronger Finland. Donate to Aalto University Privacy notice Cookie policy Feedback Accessibility statement Cookie settings Suomeksi Svenska English"
