    "https://www.aalto.fi/en/open-positions/assistant-professor-power-electronics": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Power Electronics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Power Electronics | Aalto University Skip to main content Sign of Change Sign of Change Donate Apply to Aalto Valitse sivuston kieli / Välj webbplatsens språk / Select site language EN FI Suomeksi SV Svenska EN English Search Log in Menu Close menu Student Guide For personnel Aalto community members please log in to see internal content Admissions and studies Apply to Aalto Find a study programme How to apply Scholarships and tuition fees Bachelor's admissions (programmes in Finnish and Swedish) Bachelor’s admissions (programmes in English) Master's admissions Doctoral admissions Campus life Events for applicants Chat with students Subscribe to newsletter Contact admission services Founder School: from students to founders Lifewide Learning Exchange students Research and art About our research and art Tenure track career system Doctoral education Research and learning infrastructures Research portal research.aalto.fi Rankings Schools and departments Schools School of Arts, Design and Architecture School of Business School of Chemical Engineering School of Electrical Engineering School of Engineering School of Science Departments Accounting & Business Law Applied Physics Architecture Art and Media Bioproducts and Biosystems Built Environment Chemical and Metallurgical Engineering Chemistry and Materials Science Civil Engineering Computer Science Design Economics Electrical Engineering and Automation Electronics and Nanoengineering Film, Television and Scenography Finance Industrial Engineering and Management Information and Communications Engineering Information and Service Management Management Studies Marketing Mathematics and Systems Analysis Energy and Mechanical Engineering Neuroscience and Biomedical Engineering Other units Language Centre Library - Learning Centre Collaboration Collaborate with us For alumni Corporate collaboration Aalto networking platform Entrepreneurship and innovations Cooperation with HEI and research institutes Collaboration with cities and regions Support us News and events Highlights News Events Aalto University Magazine OurBlogs Podcasts About us About Aalto University Our strategy Sustainability Code of Conduct Aalto Handbook Campus People and contact information For the media Careers Tools and services All tools (requires login) All services Most used tools Aalto AI Assistant Abacus-accounting Abacus-planning Asio (booking.aalto.fi) Halli Marketing Cloud MOT Kielipalvelu (language service) Neo People hub Phone book PowerBI report finder Salesforce (Service platform) Tiima Webmail Webropol Workday Most used services AI in Aalto Communications services HR services IT Services Learning services Occupational health Research and innovation services Teacher's Handbook Travel services For students Sisu MyCourses MyStudies Browse all courses Safety and emergencies Emergencies Safety and security observations Cyber Security Cyber Security incident report Other Aalto Space Aalto University Shop Brand library and design system Lunch menus EN FI SV Apply to Aalto Donate Student Guide For personnel Aalto community members please log in to see internal content Log in Search Open positions Assistant Professor, Power Electronics 9.10.2026 Application closes on 29.11.2026 Unit School of Electrical Engineering Job category Faculty, professors Aalto University is where science and art meet technology and business. We shape a sustainable future by making research breakthroughs in and across our disciplines, sparking the game changers of tomorrow and creating novel solutions to major global challenges. Our community is made up of 13 000 students, 400 professors and close to 4 500 other faculty and staff working on our dynamic campus in Espoo, Greater Helsinki, Finland. Diversity is part of who we are, and we actively work to ensure our community’s diversity and inclusiveness. This is why we warmly encourage qualified candidates from all backgrounds to join our community. The School of Electrical Engineering invites applications for an Assistant Professor in Power Electronics at the Department of Electrical Engineering and Automation . The position is full-time and fixed-term at the assistant professor level of the Aalto University tenure track system . The tenure track offers a supported pathway towards a permanent professorship, with advancement based on achievements and potential assessed against Aalto’s tenure track evaluation criteria . Your research environment You will join the Department of Electrical Engineering and Automation at Aalto University’s School of Electrical Engineering . The department brings together expertise in electrical power systems and energy conversion, control and automation, robotics, and electronic and digital systems. We combine fundamental research with experimental work and close collaboration with industry to address scientific and technological challenges. Power electronics is central to the department’s research and education in electrical energy conversion. The department's research spans the whole chain from power semiconductor devices to electric machine drives and power system applications, offering opportunities for collaboration at every level of this chain. Across Aalto, further collaboration opportunities include electrochemical conversion and storage, mechatronics and space technology, supported by university-wide initiatives such as the Aalto House of Energy Transition and the Aalto House of AI . The department's research groups also have access to the ePowerHub laboratory space. Finland's strong industrial power electronics ecosystem, with major players in electric drives, charging technologies and the wider electrification of industry and transport, provides a stimulating setting for research with practical impact. Your role Your research will advance the design of power electronic converters, from novel main-circuit topologies, passive components, and gate-driver systems to prototyping and experimental validation. The overarching aim is to enable efficient, reliable, compact, and resource-conscious electrical energy conversion. Relevant application areas include electric drives, charging, energy storage, electricity-to-heat conversion, data centres and sustainable transport, with increasing demands for efficiency, power density, reliability, and integration. Wide-bandgap semiconductor technologies and AI-assisted design and optimisation methods are among the key opportunities for progress. You will establish an independent research direction that complements and strengthens the department’s existing expertise. You will build your own research group, acquire external research funding, supervise doctoral researchers and master’s students, and develop collaborations with academic and industrial partners in Finland and internationally. You will also contribute to teaching and curriculum development in power electronics and electrical engineering at bachelor’s and master’s levels. The typical teaching load is two courses per year on converter topologies and related topics. The details will be discussed with other teaching staff based on the degree program needs. We value research-based teaching that connects theoretical understanding with converter design, laboratory work, and practical applications. Your profile We seek a promising researcher with a strong foundation in power electronics and the potential to develop into an internationally recognised academic leader. You should demonstrate expertise in one or more of the following closely related areas: Power electronic converter topologies, main-circuit design, analysis, and modelling; AI-assisted design, optimisation, and automated synthesis of power electronic converters; High-frequency and high-power-density power conversion, including magnetic components and passives integration; Power electronics hardware design, integration, prototyping, and experimental validation; Application of wide-bandgap power semiconductors, including silicon carbide (SiC) and gallium nitride (GaN). We expect you to have: A doctoral degree in electrical engineering, power electronics or a closely related field; Evidence of high-quality research through publications in leading international journals and conferences, assessed in relation to your career stage; A clear and original research vision, with the potential to establish an independent research programme and attract external funding; Experience in teaching and supervision, or demonstrated potential and motivation to develop into an excellent university teacher and supervisor; The ability to build productive collaborations within academia and with industry; Excellent communication skills in English and the ability to work effectively in an international, multidisciplinary environment. Experience in industrial research and development, collaborative research projects, or translating research findings into practical applications will be considered an advantage. We value a commitment to developing your pedagogical competence and contributing to an inclusive academic community. Assessment at the assistant professor level will emphasise the quality of your achievements, the originality of your research vision and your potential for future development, taking your career stage into account. What we offer Starting package and grant-writing support to help establish your research group; Opportunities for multidisciplinary collaboration across Aalto University and with industrial and academic partners; A stimulating environment for research and teaching, with highly motivated students; Support for professional development, including teaching and academic leadership; An international community committed to equality, inclusion and wellbeing; A competitive salary based on your experience and qualifications and the Aalto University salary system; Occupational healthcare and support for settling into life in Finland. The position is based at Aalto University’s Otaniemi campus in Espoo, in the Helsinki metropolitan area. Learn more about working at Aalto and living in Finland . Ready to apply? Please submit your application by November 29, 2026 , through Aalto University’s recruitment system using the “Apply now” link. Please include the following documents in English and in PDF format: Cover letter describing your motivation and suitability for the position. Curriculum vitae , including contact information, relevant researcher identifiers, links to professional profiles, and contact details for two referees. List of publications , highlighting your five most significant publications, and briefly explaining your contribution to each. Research statement (max 5 pages) describing your main research achievements, future research plans, and how your research would complement and strengthen power electronics at Aalto. Please also outline potential funding sources and opportunities for collaboration. Teaching statement (2 pages) describing your teaching and supervision experience and your educational approach. Please see the guidelines here . Aalto University employees should apply through the internal Workday recruitment system using their existing accounts. External expert reviewers will support the evaluation of applicants. The most suitable candidates will be invited for interviews and teaching demonstrations. If you wish to hear more about the position, you can reach out to the chair of the departmental committee, Professor Tomi Laurila (tomi.laurila@aalto.fi).  For questions concerning the recruitment process, please contact HR partner Camilla Hanganpää (camilla.hanganpaa@aalto.fi). More about Aalto University: Aalto.fi youtube.com/user/aaltouniversity linkedin.com/school/aalto-university/ www.facebook.com/aaltouniversity instagram.com/aaltouniversity To view information about Workday Accessibility, please click here . Please see more of our Open Positions here. Interested? Apply now! Updated: 9.10.2026 Published: 9.10.2026 Share URL copied! Home Open positions Assistant Professor, Power Electronics Sign of Change Aalto University P.O. Box 11000 (Otakaari 1B) FI-00076 AALTO Switchboard: +358 9 47001 Follow us: Facebook LinkedIn Bluesky Instagram Youtube Snapchat Blogs Quicklinks Research and artistic outputs Library – Learning Centre Admissions Alumni Media IT services Open University Aalto University Shop Site index Latest News Events Careers Contact Campus maps Contact information Ethical channel – Whistleblowing For students Student Guide Webmail MyCourses MyStudies Sisu Together towards a better world. Support new ideas, research, work and leadership development towards a stronger Finland. Donate to Aalto University Privacy notice Cookie policy Feedback Accessibility statement Cookie settings Suomeksi Svenska English"
