    "https://www.aalto.fi/en/open-positions/postdoctoral-researcher-in-cloud-and-network-computing": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral researcher in Cloud and Network Computing",
      "description": "Postdoctoral researcher in Cloud and Network Computing | Aalto University Skip to main content Sign of Change Sign of Change Donate Apply to Aalto Valitse sivuston kieli / Välj webbplatsens språk / Select site language EN FI Suomeksi SV Svenska EN English Search Log in Menu Close menu Student Guide For personnel Aalto community members please log in to see internal content Admissions and studies Apply to Aalto Find a study programme How to apply Scholarships and tuition fees Bachelor's admissions (programmes in Finnish and Swedish) Bachelor’s admissions (programmes in English) Master's admissions Doctoral admissions Campus life Events for applicants Chat with students Subscribe to newsletter Contact admission services Founder School: from students to founders Lifewide Learning Exchange students Research and art About our research and art Tenure track career system Doctoral education Research and learning infrastructures Research portal research.aalto.fi Rankings Schools and departments Schools School of Arts, Design and Architecture School of Business School of Chemical Engineering School of Electrical Engineering School of Engineering School of Science Departments Accounting & Business Law Applied Physics Architecture Art and Media Bioproducts and Biosystems Built Environment Chemical and Metallurgical Engineering Chemistry and Materials Science Civil Engineering Computer Science Design Economics Electrical Engineering and Automation Electronics and Nanoengineering Film, Television and Scenography Finance Industrial Engineering and Management Information and Communications Engineering Information and Service Management Management Studies Marketing Mathematics and Systems Analysis Energy and Mechanical Engineering Neuroscience and Biomedical Engineering Other units Language Centre Library - Learning Centre Collaboration Collaborate with us For alumni Corporate collaboration Aalto networking platform Entrepreneurship and innovations Cooperation with HEI and research institutes Collaboration with cities and regions Support us News and events Highlights News Events Aalto University Magazine OurBlogs Podcasts About us About Aalto University Our strategy Sustainability Code of Conduct Aalto Handbook Campus People and contact information For the media Careers Tools and services All tools (requires login) All services Most used tools Aalto AI Assistant Abacus-accounting Abacus-planning Asio (booking.aalto.fi) Halli Marketing Cloud MOT Kielipalvelu (language service) Neo People hub Phone book PowerBI report finder Salesforce (Service platform) Tiima Webmail Webropol Workday Most used services AI in Aalto Communications services HR services IT Services Learning services Occupational health Research and innovation services Teacher's Handbook Travel services For students Sisu MyCourses MyStudies Browse all courses Safety and emergencies Emergencies Safety and security observations Cyber Security Cyber Security incident report Other Aalto Space Aalto University Shop Brand library and design system Lunch menus EN FI SV Apply to Aalto Donate Student Guide For personnel Aalto community members please log in to see internal content Log in Search Open positions Postdoctoral researcher in Cloud and Network Computing 21.10.2026 Application closes on 30.12.2026 Unit School of Electrical Engineering Job category Other teaching and research personnel We are recruiting one postdoctoral researcher to join our team. Your role You will define and lead a research agenda at the intersection of multimodal large language models and networking, examples include semantic and context-aware networking, resource management in edge computing systems, and AI-native network control. An important part of the role is designing and building realistic simulators to generate data, evaluate algorithms, and study network behavior under dynamic conditions. Our ongoing project funded through NSF and RCF joint project provides a motivating public-safety communication context. You will work closely with the PI and with international collaborators, and will take a leading role in mentoring PhD and Master's students while advancing your independent research profile. The position requires PhD in computer science, telecommunications / electrical engineering, or a related field Excellent research track record in networking or MLLMs or LLMs Demonstrated experience in building and designing simulation environments Merit: Experience in developing algorithms for resource management Ability to provide guidance and mentorship to doctoral researchers and master’s students, and collaborate with diverse research groups What we offer You will become a part of the Cloud and Network Computing group, headed by assistant professor Gopika Premsankar. Our group is dedicated to advancing research in networked systems, primarily focused on lowering the environmental footprint of such systems while enhancing performance and reliability. The NSF-RCF joint project provides opportunities for visiting collaborators in North Carolina State University and Penn State University. The role is fully funded for 2 years, with the possibility of a longer stay. You will receive a competitive salary, starting at approximately 4220 EUR / month for a postdoctoral researcher. The contract includes comprehensive occupational health benefits. Application documents To apply, please share the following application materials with us through our recruitment site (\"Apply now!” button at the bottom of the page): A CV A short letter of motivation, at most 1 page, which describes your interest and motivation (please try to include details that are not part of your CV and directly address the requirements listed above) Sample code for simulations, preferably on a code repository Names and email addresses of those who could provide a reference letter (at least two are required). They will be contacted directly at a later stage in the application process. Publication list with 1 or 2 key publications highlighted. At the end of the list, please describe in one paragraph the relevance of the highlighted publication(s) to the role. Application process The application deadline is December 30th, 2026 (23:59 EET). We will go through applications in batches, and we will invite suitable candidates to interview already before the application deadline. The position will be closed once the position is filled. Please note: Aalto University’s employees should apply for the position via our internal HR system Workday (Internal Jobs) by using their existing Workday user account (not via the external webpage for open positions). More information For more information about the position, please contact Gopika Premsankar (gopika.premsankar@aalto.fi).  For questions about the application process, please contact HR Advisor Johanna Haapalainen at hr-elec@aalto.fi. Why Finland and why this group Aalto University provides a vibrant and collaborative environment. We work in a hybrid way, and the primary workplace is Otaniemi, Espoo. The Otaniemi campus is a thriving and connected community of 100 nationalities, 16,000 students and 5,200 employees. Life at the campus is vibrant and filled with amazing architecture, calming nature, and a variety of cafes, restaurants, services and good transport connections. Finland is a great place for living – it is a safe, politically stable and well-organized Nordic society. For more information about living in Finland: https://www.aalto.fi/en/careers-at-aalto/living-in-finland & https://www.aalto.fi/en/services/welcome-to-aalto-university-and-finland-info-package Read more about working at Aalto: https://www.aalto.fi/en/careers-at-aalto and check out our new virtual campus experience: https://virtualtour.aalto.fi More about Aalto University: Aalto.fi youtube.com/user/aaltouniversity linkedin.com/school/aalto-university/ www.facebook.com/aaltouniversity instagram.com/aaltouniversity To view information about Workday Accessibility, please click here . Please see more of our Open Positions here. Interested? Apply now! Updated: 21.10.2026 Published: 21.10.2026 Share URL copied! Home Open positions Postdoctoral researcher in Cloud and Network Computing Sign of Change Aalto University P.O. Box 11000 (Otakaari 1B) FI-00076 AALTO Switchboard: +358 9 47001 Follow us: Facebook LinkedIn Bluesky Instagram Youtube Snapchat Blogs Quicklinks Research and artistic outputs Library – Learning Centre Admissions Alumni Media IT services Open University Aalto University Shop Site index Latest News Events Careers Contact Campus maps Contact information Ethical channel – Whistleblowing For students Student Guide Webmail MyCourses MyStudies Sisu Together towards a better world. Support new ideas, research, work and leadership development towards a stronger Finland. Donate to Aalto University Privacy notice Cookie policy Feedback Accessibility statement Cookie settings Suomeksi Svenska English"
    },
    "https://www.aalto.fi/en/open-positions/sales-assistant-aalto-university-shop": {
      "title": "Sales assistant, Aalto University Shop",
      "description": "Sales assistant, Aalto University Shop | Aalto University Skip to main content Sign of Change Sign of Change Donate Apply to Aalto Valitse sivuston kieli / Välj webbplatsens språk / Select site language EN FI Suomeksi SV Svenska EN English Search Log in Menu Close menu Student Guide For personnel Aalto community members please log in to see internal content Admissions and studies Apply to Aalto Find a study programme How to apply Scholarships and tuition fees Bachelor's admissions (programmes in Finnish and Swedish) Bachelor’s admissions (programmes in English) Master's admissions Doctoral admissions Campus life Events for applicants Chat with students Subscribe to newsletter Contact admission services Founder School: from students to founders Lifewide Learning Exchange students Research and art About our research and art Tenure track career system Doctoral education Research and learning infrastructures Research portal research.aalto.fi Rankings Schools and departments Schools School of Arts, Design and Architecture School of Business School of Chemical Engineering School of Electrical Engineering School of Engineering School of Science Departments Accounting & Business Law Applied Physics Architecture Art and Media Bioproducts and Biosystems Built Environment Chemical and Metallurgical Engineering Chemistry and Materials Science Civil Engineering Computer Science Design Economics Electrical Engineering and Automation Electronics and Nanoengineering Film, Television and Scenography Finance Industrial Engineering and Management Information and Communications Engineering Information and Service Management Management Studies Marketing Mathematics and Systems Analysis Energy and Mechanical Engineering Neuroscience and Biomedical Engineering Other units Language Centre Library - Learning Centre Collaboration Collaborate with us For alumni Corporate collaboration Aalto networking platform Entrepreneurship and innovations Cooperation with HEI and research institutes Collaboration with cities and regions Support us News and events Highlights News Events Aalto University Magazine OurBlogs Podcasts About us About Aalto University Our strategy Sustainability Code of Conduct Aalto Handbook Campus People and contact information For the media Careers Tools and services All tools (requires login) All services Most used tools Aalto AI Assistant Abacus-accounting Abacus-planning Asio (booking.aalto.fi) Halli Marketing Cloud MOT Kielipalvelu (language service) Neo People hub Phone book PowerBI report finder Salesforce (Service platform) Tiima Webmail Webropol Workday Most used services AI in Aalto Communications services HR services IT Services Learning services Occupational health Research and innovation services Teacher's Handbook Travel services For students Sisu MyCourses MyStudies Browse all courses Safety and emergencies Emergencies Safety and security observations Cyber Security Cyber Security incident report Other Aalto Space Aalto University Shop Brand library and design system Lunch menus EN FI SV Apply to Aalto Donate Student Guide For personnel Aalto community members please log in to see internal content Log in Search Open positions Sales assistant, Aalto University Shop 21.10.2026 Application closes on 8.11.2026 Unit University Units Job category Services Aalto University is recruiting its own bachelor’s and master’s degree students to join the student employees team at Communications Services. Student employees work as student ambassadors in the university through a variety of roles, such as in student marketing, leading campus tours, representing Aalto at events and working with retail and branded merchandise. We are currently looking for 4-6 students interested in a shop-based role, working as sales assistants and helping provide a welcoming, high-quality customer experience at the Aalto University Shop. Sales Assistant to Aalto University Shop in Otaniemi, Espoo We are looking for an energetic and outgoing person to join our shop team and help develop our retail culture and experience. You will be part of a team that serves and sells to both external and internal customers in our store. As a Sales Assistant at the Aalto University Shop, you will: Provide excellent customer service and experience in store, by email and phone Assist customers in finding what they need Ensure store aesthetics and visual merchandising are up to standard Restock the store Handle store deliveries Process web shop orders Represent Aalto University Deliver welcoming services and help visitors find what they need What’s in it for you? We offer you an exciting opportunity to be involved in a rewarding customer-centric team where your ideas and skills may help develop and shape our future retail experience. In order to succeed , we expect that you are or have: Proactive attitude towards work, and a get-it-done mindset Passionate about customer service Have general knowledge and an interest in sales Good people skills and the ability to work as part of a team as well as alone Ability to manage time and handle multiple tasks simultaneously Good communication skills Good English and Finnish language skills You are currently a bachelor's or master's degree student at Aalto University This is a part-time, fixed term contract term until 31.12.2027. Working hours: 30-60 hours a month. Starting date: 04.01.2027 For more information about this position, please contact Retail Operations Manager, Daniel Abild on October 26th  between 14:00 and 15:00, or on October 28th between 11:30-12:30 on tel. 050 441 2878. Please submit your English application and CV through our recruitment system by 8 November 2026. More about Aalto University: Aalto.fi youtube.com/user/aaltouniversity linkedin.com/school/aalto-university/ www.facebook.com/aaltouniversity instagram.com/aaltouniversity To view information about Workday Accessibility, please click here . Please see more of our Open Positions here. Interested? Apply now! Updated: 21.10.2026 Published: 21.10.2026 Share URL copied! Home Open positions Sales assistant, Aalto University Shop Sign of Change Aalto University P.O. Box 11000 (Otakaari 1B) FI-00076 AALTO Switchboard: +358 9 47001 Follow us: Facebook LinkedIn Bluesky Instagram Youtube Snapchat Blogs Quicklinks Research and artistic outputs Library – Learning Centre Admissions Alumni Media IT services Open University Aalto University Shop Site index Latest News Events Careers Contact Campus maps Contact information Ethical channel – Whistleblowing For students Student Guide Webmail MyCourses MyStudies Sisu Together towards a better world. Support new ideas, research, work and leadership development towards a stronger Finland. Donate to Aalto University Privacy notice Cookie policy Feedback Accessibility statement Cookie settings Suomeksi Svenska English"
